<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>9.10.2: Expanding from Factored Form to Standard Form</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02499</md:content-id>
    <md:title>9.10.2: Expanding from Factored Form to Standard Form</md:title>
    <md:uuid>e613e98c-3c47-4de8-8d8b-231d057b2969</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <title>Warm Up Activity</title>
      <para id="para-00001">Recall learning how to identify and factor perfect square trinomials in Unit 6. Here are some perfect squares in factored and standard forms, and an expression showing how the two forms are related.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">Study the first few examples in rows 1 and 2. Create a similar table to the one modeled below. Copy the table (or use a copy provided by your teacher) and then complete the missing numbers in rows 3 – 6 in the rest of the table.</para>
      <table class="os-raise-wideadjustedtable" id="table-00001">
        <tgroup cols="4">
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <entry><emphasis>Row</emphasis></entry>
              <entry><emphasis>Factored Form</emphasis></entry>
              <entry><emphasis> </emphasis></entry>
              <entry><emphasis>Standard Form</emphasis></entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00003">1</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00004">\((x+4)^2\)</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00005">\((1x)^2+2(1x)(4)+4^2\)</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00006">\(x^2+8x+16\)</para>
              </entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00007">2</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00008">\((2x+5)^2\)</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00009">\((2x)^2+2(2x)(5)+5^2\)</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00010">\(4x^2+20x+25\)</para>
              </entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00011">3</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00012">\((3x-4)^2\)</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00013">\((3x)^2+2(\_\_\_\;x)(\_\_\_)+(\_\_\_)^2\)</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00014">\(9x^2−24x+16\)</para>
              </entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00015">4</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00016">\((5x + \_\_\_)^2\)</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00017">\((\_\_\_\;x)^2+2(\_\_\_\;x)(\_\_\_)+(\_\_\_)^2\)</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00018">\(25x^2+30x + \_\_\_\)</para>
              </entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00019">5</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00020">\((kx+m)^2\)</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00021">\((\_\_\_\;x)^2+2(\_\_\_\;x)(\_\_\_)+(\_\_\_)^2\)</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00022">\((\_\_\_)^2x^2+ \_\_\_\;x+ (\_\_\_)^2\)</para>
              </entry>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00001">
        <item>Enter the missing values from row 3.</item>
      </list>
      <table class="os-raise-wideadjustedtable" id="table-00002">
        <tgroup cols="4">
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <entry><emphasis>Row</emphasis></entry>
              <entry><emphasis>Factored Form</emphasis></entry>
              <entry><emphasis> </emphasis></entry>
              <entry><emphasis>Standard Form</emphasis></entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00023">3</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00024">\((3x-4)^2\)</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00025">\((3x)^2+2(\_\_\_\;x)(\_\_\_)+(\_\_\_)^2\) \((3x)^2+2(\;\underline{\;\mathbf a\boldsymbol.\;}\;x)(\underline{\;\mathbf b\boldsymbol.\;})+(\underline{\;\mathbf c\boldsymbol.\;})^2\)</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00026">\(9x^2−24x+16\)</para>
              </entry>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
      <exercise id="dad71f78-dfbe-4ce8-84f6-174d080677d9" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00027">Enter the missing value of a.</para>
          <para id="para-00028">What is the missing value of a?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00029">Correct! 3</para>
          <para id="para-00030">The correct answer is 3.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="f8bd948f-e55c-410a-a56c-08a864670510" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00031">Enter the missing value of b.</para>
          <para id="para-00032">What is the missing value of b?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00033">Correct! -4</para>
          <para id="para-00034">The correct answer is -4.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_448b88de-78d0-428d-8320-b5d463cd72fe" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00035">Enter the missing value of c.</para>
          <para id="para-00036">What is the missing value of c?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00037">Correct! -4</para>
          <para id="para-00038">The correct answer is -4.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00002">
        <item>Enter the missing values from row 4.</item>
      </list>
      <table class="os-raise-wideadjustedtable" id="table-00003">
        <tgroup cols="4">
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <entry><emphasis>Row</emphasis></entry>
              <entry><emphasis>Factored Form</emphasis></entry>
              <entry><emphasis> </emphasis></entry>
              <entry><emphasis>Standard Form</emphasis></entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00039">4</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00040">\((5x + \_\_\_)^2\) \((5x + \underline{\;\mathbf a\boldsymbol.\;})^2\)</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00041">\((\_\_\_\;x)^2+2(\_\_\_\;x)(\_\_\_)+(\_\_\_)^2\) \((\underline{\;\mathbf b\boldsymbol.\;}\;x)^2+2(\underline{\;\mathbf c\boldsymbol.\;}\;x)(\underline{\;\mathbf d\boldsymbol.\;})+(\underline{\;\mathbf e\boldsymbol.\;})^2\)</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00042">\(25x^2+30x + \_\_\_ \) \(25x^2+30x + \underline{\;\mathbf f\boldsymbol.\;}\)</para>
              </entry>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
      <exercise id="a6b625d4-10aa-4150-ae58-791cf77361d7" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00043">Enter the missing value of a.</para>
          <para id="para-00044">What is the missing value of a?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00045">Correct! 3</para>
          <para id="para-00046">The correct answer is 3.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="d92d34c8-3b69-4bb0-b4de-ef514d6ed71b" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00005">
          <para id="para-00047">Enter the missing value of b.</para>
          <para id="para-00048">What is the missing value of b?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00005">
          <para id="para-00049">Correct! 5</para>
          <para id="para-00050">The correct answer is 5.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="eaa30f11-95c5-4267-a258-982376579f21" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00006">
          <para id="para-00051">Enter the missing value of c.</para>
          <para id="para-00052">What is the missing value of c?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00006">
          <para id="para-00053">Correct! 5</para>
          <para id="para-00054">The correct answer is 5.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_3b4c63db-6340-4d1c-86e9-ade95ce69455" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00007">
          <para id="para-00055">Enter the missing value of d.</para>
          <para id="para-00056">What is the missing value of d?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00007">
          <para id="para-00057">Correct! 3</para>
          <para id="para-00058">The correct answer is 3.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_1572d1cf-b757-4b6f-a8a0-e625692b3f7a" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00008">
          <para id="para-00059">Enter the missing value of e.</para>
          <para id="para-00060">What is the missing value of e?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00008">
          <para id="para-00061">Correct! 3</para>
          <para id="para-00062">The correct answer is 3.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_8a1ec2b2-3c19-48e7-9802-3a07306b4efd" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00009">
          <para id="para-00063">Enter the missing value of f.</para>
          <para id="para-00064">What is the missing value of f?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00009">
          <para id="para-00065">Correct! 9</para>
          <para id="para-00066">The correct answer is 9.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00003">
        <item>Enter the missing values from row 5.</item>
      </list>
      <table class="os-raise-wideadjustedtable" id="table-00004">
        <tgroup cols="4">
          <tbody>
            <row>
              <entry><emphasis>Row</emphasis></entry>
              <entry><emphasis>Factored Form</emphasis></entry>
              <entry><emphasis> </emphasis></entry>
              <entry><emphasis>Standard Form</emphasis></entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00067">5</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00068">\((kx+m)^2\)</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00069">\((\_\_\_\;x)^2+2(\_\_\_\;x)(\_\_\_)+(\_\_\_)^2\) \((\underline{\;\mathbf a\boldsymbol.\;}\;x)^2+2(\underline{\;\mathbf b\boldsymbol.\;}\;x)(\underline{\;\mathbf c\boldsymbol.\;})+(\underline{\;\mathbf d\boldsymbol.\;})^2\)</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00070">\((\_\_\_)^2x^2 + \_\_\_\;x + (\_\_\_)^2\) \((\underline{\;\mathbf e\boldsymbol.\;})^2x^2 + \underline{\;\mathbf f\boldsymbol.\;} x + (\underline{\;\mathbf g\boldsymbol.\;} )^2\)</para>
              </entry>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
      <exercise id="_4605d8cb-adc0-47e9-9ddc-e7b5f0e8a1db" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00010">
          <para id="para-00071">Enter the missing value of a.</para>
          <para id="para-00072">What is the missing value of a?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00010">
          <para id="para-00073">Correct! \(k\)</para>
          <para id="para-00074">The correct answer is \(k\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="d0547d87-7153-4f40-9a1b-06ba89b584bf" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00011">
          <para id="para-00075">Enter the missing value of b.</para>
          <para id="para-00076">What is the missing value of b?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00011">
          <para id="para-00077">Correct! \(k\)</para>
          <para id="para-00078">The correct answer is \(k\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="e65eb74e-65af-419b-8402-a7feb616f885" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00012">
          <para id="para-00079">Enter the missing value of c.</para>
          <para id="para-00080">What is the missing value of c?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00012">
          <para id="para-00081">Correct! \(m\)</para>
          <para id="para-00082">The correct answer is \(m\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_37175167-199e-4386-a447-8ea590d9bf66" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00013">
          <para id="para-00083">Enter the missing value of d.</para>
          <para id="para-00084">What is the missing value of d?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00013">
          <para id="para-00085">Correct! \(m\)</para>
          <para id="para-00086">The correct answer is \(m\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_165fc1b2-9a9c-4672-be9f-506c9a8e9c4c" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00014">
          <para id="para-00087">Enter the missing value of e.</para>
          <para id="para-00088">What is the missing value of e?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00014">
          <para id="para-00089">Correct! \(k\)</para>
          <para id="para-00090">The correct answer is \(k\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_7f40aa1b-830a-44d8-9b8b-72ec21ac5abc" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00015">
          <para id="para-00091">Enter the missing value of f.</para>
          <para id="para-00092">What is the missing value of f?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00015">
          <para id="para-00093">Correct! \(2km\)</para>
          <para id="para-00094">The correct answer is \(2km\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="_3b96c095-cbc3-4a4c-8611-b264e978aefa" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00016">
          <para id="para-00095">Enter the missing value of g.</para>
          <para id="para-00096">What is the missing value of g?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00016">
          <para id="para-00097">Correct! \(m\)</para>
          <para id="para-00098">The correct answer is \(m\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00017">
          <para id="para-00099">Look at the expression in the last row of the table. If \(ax^2+bx+c\) is equivalent to \((kx+m)^2\), how are \(a\), \(b\), and \(c\) related to \(k\) and \(m\)?</para>
          <para id="para-00100">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00017">
          <para id="para-00101">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00102">\(a=k^2\), \(b=2km\), and \(c=m^2\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
